      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's getting more detailed, but the word count is still quite low. The metric for this repo is pretty strict—if we don't hit a certain threshold, the automated system flags it as \"insufficient documentation.\"\n\nI know I said not to pad it, but we really need to push that length up to ensure we pass the automated check. Try to go much deeper. You could add a section on \"Prerequisite Troubleshooting,\" an \"Understanding the Command Lifecycle\" section, or maybe even a \"Glossary of Terms\" at the bottom. Just make sure it stays somewhat relevant to the tool so it doesn't look totally fake, but we definitely need more volume to satisfy the metric.",
