    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**SkyLink CLI Comprehensive Quick Start Guide**\n\nTo successfully bootstrap your development environment, verify that the Docker daemon is fully operational, as this is crucial for standardized container deployment. Furthermore, Node.js v18 or newer must be present, guaranteeing compatibility with the CLI's dependencies and modern JavaScript features. Installation is executed via `npm install -g skylink-cli`, which places the binary onto your global path for easy access. Upon installation, run `skylink login` to securely authenticate; this initiates a token exchange with our API server. When you are ready, executing `skylink deploy --env staging` triggers the lifecycle: the CLI packages your assets, builds the necessary Docker image, and pushes it to the designated staging Kubernetes cluster. For troubleshooting, if Docker fails, check service status or if Node.js is unavailable, verify the installed version using `node -v`.",
      "source": "target",
